The models include or were derived from the following third-party material.

- mMiniLMv2 (Multilingual-MiniLM), Microsoft — https://github.com/microsoft/unilm/tree/master/minilm
  The four models start from mMiniLMv2-L6-H384; the vocabulary is pruned and the layers are compressed per size.
- XLM-R SentencePiece tokenizer, Facebook AI — https://github.com/facebookresearch/fairseq/tree/main/examples/xlmr
  The tokenizer files are the XLM-R tokenizer with its vocabulary pruned to the pieces used in training.
- Teacher models used only to produce training targets (not distributed): mDeBERTa-v3-base (Microsoft, MIT License) and
  XLM-RoBERTa-large (Facebook AI, MIT License), fine-tuned by newmean.ai.

Training data: synthetic text generated by newmean.ai with Claude models; no third-party dataset was used for training.
